          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: el olivo",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "el olivo — \"the olive tree\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "En el campo hay miles de olivos. There are thousands of olive trees in the countryside."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The fruit is la aceituna; the oil is el aceite de oliva."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "olivo is inherited from Vulgar Latin olīvus, from Latin olīva, which comes from Greek elaía \"olive\" (EtymDB)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
